 1069 "q-112208" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186247250 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186247250 #edb/ref 1071 "Find the coordinates of the vector $x$ relative to the basis $B=\\{{b}_{1},{b}_{2},{b}_{3}\\},$ where\n\n$$\n{b}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}],\\,{b}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],\\,{b}_{3}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}],\\,x=[\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nIf $[x]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{aligned}]$ then what is the value of ${x}_{2}?$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186247250 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "438d91ee-b10a-5c27-8e0b-9fc621fd3a05" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186247250 #edb/ref 1074 "Remember, the order of the vectors in a basis is important.\n\nNotice that \n\n$$\n{{[\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{x}={{(\\,2\\,)}_{⏟}}_{{x}_{1}}\\cdot {{[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{{b}_{1}}+{{(\\,3\\,)}_{⏟}}_{{x}_{2}}\\cdot {{[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{{b}_{2}}+{{(\\,6\\,)}_{⏟}}_{{x}_{3}}\\cdot {{[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{{b}_{3}}\n$$\n\nwhich means that\n\n$$\nx=2\\cdot {b}_{1}+3\\cdot {b}_{2}+6\\cdot {b}_{3}\n$$\n\nand therefore \n\n$$\n[x]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}],\n$$\n\nFinally, ${x}_{2}=3.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186256980 #edb/ref 1080 "f(x,y,z)=x{y}^{2}{z}^{3}+yz-{e}^{z}+C" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186256980 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186256980 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "1602f189-0d28-56ae-9dd9-e128132e6ed0" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186257529 #edb/ref 1080 "f(x,y,z)=xyz-y{e}^{z}+C" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186257529 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186257529 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "56a824e1-89ad-5b9f-9d90-0a15c3c6afec" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186257944 #edb/ref 1080 "f